      explain: "A research agent combines several patterns: **planning** (break the question into sub-questions), **parallel search** (subagents or parallel tool calls per sub-question), **reading and extraction** (pull relevant passages with source metadata), **iteration** (follow new leads until coverage is sufficient or the budget is spent), and **synthesis with citations**. Quality depends most on source handling: prefer primary and authoritative sources, record exactly which passage supports each claim, and say when sources disagree or are missing. Measure **citation coverage** (the share of factual sentences with at least one citation) and **citation correctness** (whether the cited passage actually supports the sentence).",
